1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,707
This is STAT 331, video 1, part b. The topic is covariance and correlation. Part a covered the mean and the variance.

2
00:00:10,157 --> 00:00:33,410
After this video, you can calculate a covariance with both forms, and use its properties. You can find the variance of a sum and of a difference. You can calculate the sample covariance and the correlation by hand. And you can write the correlation with the sums S x y, S x x, and S y y. All of regression uses these sums.

3
00:00:33,860 --> 00:00:55,193
Covariance measures how two random variables change together. The covariance of X and Y is the expectation of X minus its mean, times Y minus its mean. As an example, take the first 5 people as a whole population. Pick one person at random, each with probability one fifth.

4
00:00:55,643 --> 00:01:13,841
The purple lines are the means, 4093 and 1406.8. They cut the plane into four parts. Top right, both deviations are positive. Bottom left, both are negative. In the other two parts, the signs differ.

5
00:01:14,291 --> 00:01:27,816
Each product of deviations is the area of a rectangle from the mean point to the data point. Same signs give a positive product, in blue. Opposite signs give a negative product, in red.

6
00:01:28,266 --> 00:01:35,583
Here are the five products. Four are positive. One is negative: minus 12062.4.

7
00:01:36,033 --> 00:01:55,127
The covariance is the average product. The sum is 133363. Divide by 5: the covariance is 26672.6. It is positive, so a larger head usually goes with a heavier brain.

8
00:01:55,577 --> 00:02:01,678
The slide gives a second form. Expand the product. X times Y gives X Y.

9
00:02:02,128 --> 00:02:20,560
The other three terms are minus X times the mean of Y, minus the mean of X times Y, and plus the product of the means. Take the expectation with linearity. The means are constants. So the last three terms become minus, minus, plus the product of the means.

10
00:02:21,010 --> 00:02:30,674
Two of them cancel. So the covariance equals the expectation of X Y, minus the expectation of X times the expectation of Y.

11
00:02:31,124 --> 00:02:56,041
Check it on the 5 people. The mean of X is 4093. The mean of Y is 1406.8. The products x i y i add to 28923525. Divide by 5: the expectation of X Y is 5784705.

12
00:02:56,491 --> 00:03:15,094
Subtract 4093 times 1406.8, which is 5758032.4. The result is 26672.6. Both forms give the same covariance.

13
00:03:15,544 --> 00:03:26,189
Property 1. The covariance of X with itself is the variance of X. The rectangle has two equal sides. So it is a square of the deviation.

14
00:03:26,639 --> 00:03:48,015
Property 2. The covariance of a Y plus c with b X plus d is a b times the covariance of X and Y. The factors stretch the sides of each rectangle, so the area is multiplied by a b. A shift moves each point and its mean by the same amount. So the deviations do not change.

15
00:03:48,465 --> 00:04:00,967
Property 3. The covariance of a sum with a sum splits into pairs. Each term on the left goes with each term on the right. Two terms times two terms give four covariances.

16
00:04:01,417 --> 00:04:11,145
One more fact follows from the definition. The order does not matter: the covariance of Y and X equals the covariance of X and Y.

17
00:04:11,595 --> 00:04:18,400
The slide asks an exercise: what is the variance of X plus Y? Pause the video and try it.

18
00:04:18,850 --> 00:04:26,253
Use property 1 backwards. The variance of X plus Y is the covariance of X plus Y with itself.

19
00:04:26,703 --> 00:04:35,364
Use property 3. The grid has four cells: covariance of X with X, X with Y, Y with X, and Y with Y.

20
00:04:35,814 --> 00:04:52,433
The diagonal cells are the variances, by property 1. The two other cells are equal, because the order does not matter. So the variance of X plus Y is the variance of X, plus the variance of Y, plus 2 times the covariance.

21
00:04:52,883 --> 00:05:15,539
When X and Y are independent, the covariance is 0. Then we get property 2 of the variance. For the 5 people, the variances are 87344.4 and 16305.36. The result is 156994.96.

22
00:05:15,989 --> 00:05:30,495
For observed pairs, the sample covariance is 1 over n minus 1, times the sum of y i minus y bar, times x i minus x bar. Now we treat the 5 people as a sample.

23
00:05:30,945 --> 00:05:43,084
Find x bar, 4093, and y bar, 1406.8. Then find the deviations. Each set of deviations adds to 0.

24
00:05:43,534 --> 00:05:49,273
Multiply the two deviations of each person. These are the signed rectangles again.

25
00:05:49,723 --> 00:05:56,699
The products are the same as before. Their sum is 133363.

26
00:05:57,149 --> 00:06:15,005
Now divide by n minus 1, which is 4, not by 5. The sample covariance is 33340.75. It is larger than 26672.6 only because of the divisor.

27
00:06:15,455 --> 00:06:17,993
Now all 236 people.

28
00:06:18,443 --> 00:06:31,499
The purple lines are x bar, 3637.864, and y bar, 1284.263. They make four quadrants.

29
00:06:31,949 --> 00:06:37,901
Blue points have a positive product of deviations. Red points have a negative product.

30
00:06:38,351 --> 00:06:47,610
Quadrants 1 and 3 have 91 and 97 people. Quadrants 2 and 4 have 24 each. So most products are positive.

31
00:06:48,060 --> 00:07:11,655
The sum of the products in each quadrant is shown. The positive sums are much larger. The total is S x y, 7993433.4. Divide by 235. The sample covariance is 34014.61, in grams times cubic centimeters.

32
00:07:12,105 --> 00:07:30,046
The covariance has a problem: it depends on the units. In grams and cubic centimeters it is 34014.61. In kilograms and litres it is 0.034. The data is the same. Only the number changed.

33
00:07:30,496 --> 00:07:46,901
The correlation coefficient rho divides the covariance by the two standard deviations. The units cancel. So the correlation has no unit, and it is the same in both unit systems: 0.7937.

34
00:07:47,351 --> 00:08:01,751
For data, we use three sums. S x y is the sum of the products of deviations. S x x is the sum of squared deviations of x. S y y is the sum of squared deviations of y.

35
00:08:02,201 --> 00:08:12,612
The sample correlation r puts the sample covariance over the two sample standard deviations. Each one has a factor 1 over n minus 1.

36
00:08:13,062 --> 00:08:32,475
The square roots of the two factors multiply to 1 over n minus 1. It cancels with the numerator. So r equals S x y over the square root of S x x times S y y. The sums S x x and S x y come back in every regression lecture.

37
00:08:32,925 --> 00:08:45,213
Correlation measures the strength of a linear relationship. r is always between minus 1 and 1. Here the points are close to a rising line. r is 0.96.

38
00:08:45,663 --> 00:08:52,533
The brainhead data has r equals 0.79: a clear rising trend, with more spread.

39
00:08:52,983 --> 00:08:56,993
Here there is no linear trend. r is small: 0.12.

40
00:08:57,443 --> 00:09:03,097
Here the points fall from left to right. r is negative: minus 0.79.

41
00:09:03,547 --> 00:09:29,467
Now calculate r for the 5 people. S x y is 133363. S x x is 436722. S y y is 81526.8. So r is 133363 over the square root of their product. That is 0.7068.

42
00:09:29,917 --> 00:09:57,479
For all 236 people, S x y is 7993433.4, S x x is 30647233.7, and S y y is 3309753.7. So r is 0.7937. This is a strong positive linear relationship.

43
00:09:57,929 --> 00:10:05,140
Two more practice questions with the summaries of all 236 people. Pause the video and try them.

44
00:10:05,590 --> 00:10:29,163
Question 4. Write x minus y as x plus minus 1 times y. The grid gives the variance of X, the variance of Y, and two covariance cells. Each covariance cell has the factor minus 1. So the variance of X minus Y is the variance of X, plus the variance of Y, minus 2 times the covariance.

45
00:10:29,613 --> 00:10:47,555
Put in the numbers: 130413.76 plus 14084.06 minus 2 times 34014.61. The result is 76468.60.

46
00:10:48,005 --> 00:11:06,650
Question 5. The sample covariance is S x y over n minus 1. So S x y is 235 times 34014.61. That is 7993433.35.

47
00:11:07,100 --> 00:11:20,881
Then r is S x y over the square root of S x x times S y y. The result is 0.7937. The small difference in S x y comes from rounding.

48
00:11:21,331 --> 00:11:32,745
To recap. The outcome y is the variable whose mean we explain. The covariate x explains or predicts it. Row i gives the point x i, y i.

49
00:11:33,195 --> 00:11:51,819
Expectation is linear. The sample mean is the balance point of the data. The variance is the expected squared deviation. It equals the expectation of Y squared minus the squared expectation. The sample variance is S y y over n minus 1.

50
00:11:52,269 --> 00:12:08,183
The covariance is the expectation of X Y minus the product of the means. The variance of a sum or a difference has a term 2 times the covariance. The sample covariance is S x y over n minus 1.

51
00:12:08,633 --> 00:12:27,065
The correlation r is S x y over the square root of S x x times S y y. It has no unit. For the brainhead data, r is 0.7937. The next video reviews four distributions, and the idea of a regression line.
